# NOTE — deliberately NOT ignoring emitted TypeScript output.
#
# `tsc` ignores tsconfig.json (and its `noEmit: true`) when files are passed on
# the command line, e.g. `npx tsc src/**/*.ts`. That emits a .js next to each .ts
# source. Because Metro resolves `js` before `ts`, those artifacts then silently
# shadow the real sources and the app bundles stale code. This happened on
# 2025-10-07 and went unnoticed for ten months (22 files).
#
# src/ also contains 28 legitimate hand-written .js files, so a blanket ignore
# would be both wrong and counterproductive: if tsc ever re-emits, you want the
# stray files loud in `git status`, not hidden.
#
# Always run type checks as `npx tsc --noEmit` with no file arguments.
